    notes:
      'Built from TB1 Chapters 24, 25, 10 and 8, in the order the syllabus names them. The module covers four apparently separate technologies that share one purpose: removing the human decision from the routine parts of manufacturing. Process planning decides how a part is made, material requirements planning decides when its components are ordered, automated guided vehicles move the work between operations, and industrial robots perform the handling at each. Robotics is given the largest share because the syllabus lists it in the greatest detail, and because it is the technology whose specification errors are most expensive. All Groover page numbers are 4th-edition pages; see the edition notice in the file header.',
