      'Built from TB4 for the additive manufacturing content and TB1 for the future factory content. This split is forced by the editions supplied: the third edition of Groover that the syllabus prescribes carried a rapid prototyping chapter which the supplied fourth edition does not, so the additive material is taken from Gibson, which the syllabus also lists. The second half of the module, which the syllabus heads Future of Automated Factory, is a third edition heading; the fourth edition distributes the same material across its first chapter, on automation in production systems and manual labour in production systems, and its last, on lean production and worker involvement, with Gibson supplying the future directions material. Every unit names the source it draws on. All page numbers are from the editions actually supplied; see the edition notice in the file header.',
